d military vehicles excludes the robot, power armor and military rows. The book files Horsemanship under Pilot (printed 151-152); the catalog category is offered as General and Exotic Animals at the Pilot +15%, and Horsemanship: Cowboy is in the Cowboy category. || SECONDARY: two at levels 1, 4, 10 and 15. || MONEY: 2D6x$100 in cash/dollars is starting_money; Australian dollars equal credits. The 1D6x$500 in saleable items (text layer lD6x$500) is goods, in GM Notes. || EQUIPMENT NOT stored as rows: wide brimmed hat, gear webbing, handkerchief, durable wristwatch, silver plated knife (1D6 S.D.C.), the optional laser distancer, telescopic sight or passive nightsight scope, the sturdy S.D.C. rifle (probably bolt-action), sidearm and M.D. weapon of choice with 1D4+1 clips each or 3D4x10 bullets (text layer 3D4xlO), and the optional four-wheel drive M.D.C. vehicle of 1D6x10+35 M.D.C. (text layer !D6xlO+35). They are in GM Notes."
